<title>USA: KLM Cargo expects to carry more perishable.</title>
<headline>KLM Cargo expects to carry more perishable.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>KLM Cargo is forecasting a rise in its world-wide perishables cargo to 21,000 metric tonnes in the year to end-March from 19,500 tonnes in 1995-96.</p>
<p>KLM cargo spokesman Peter Wellhuner said 90 percent of perishables flown to John F. Kennedy Airport are flowers and plants with seafood accounting for most of the remaining 10 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;For commercial reasons however, KLM does not publish statistics for individual routes,&quot; Wellhuner said. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
